Let $\mathrm{P}(\mathrm{x}, \mathrm{y})$ be any point on the conic. Then,

\begin{array}{l}
\sqrt{(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}}=\sqrt{2}\left(\frac{x-y+1}{\sqrt{2}}\right) \\
\Rightarrow(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=(x-y+1)^{2} \\
\Rightarrow 2 x y-4 x+4 y+1=0
\end{array}

Since b and $\mathrm{C}$ are the roots of
$\begin{array}{l}
\mathrm{x}^{2}-61 \mathrm{x}+820=0, \text { so } \\
\mathrm{b}+\mathrm{c}=61, \mathrm{bc}=820 \\
\mathrm{~A}=\tan ^{-1}\left(\frac{4}{3}\right) \Rightarrow \tan \mathrm{A}=\frac{4}{3} \Rightarrow \cos \mathrm{A}=\frac{3}{5}
\end{array}
Now, using the formula,
$\cos A=\frac{b^{2}+c^{2}-a^{2}}{2 b c}\begin{aligned} \Rightarrow \mathrm{a}^{2} &=\mathrm{b}^{2}+\mathrm{c}^{2}-2 \mathrm{bc} \cos \mathrm{A} \\ &=(\mathrm{b}+\mathrm{c})^{2}-2 \mathrm{bc}-2 \mathrm{bc} \cos \mathrm{A} \\ &=(\mathrm{b}+\mathrm{c})^{2}-2 \mathrm{bc}(1+\cos \mathrm{A}) \\ &=(61)^{2}-2 \times 820\left(1+\frac{3}{5}\right) \\ &=3721-2624=1097 \end{aligned}
